  resolve  2026-12-07T05:59:00.000Z  a result is posted before it, or the whole pot refunds
  hard     2027-02-17T05:59:00.000Z  after it whatever is left refunds, so a stalled dispute never locks the pot; a 
dispute the regraders decided (2 votes for one side) never refunds but is settled on that vote, past it too, unless 
the guardian handed it to the arbiter before that vote could take effect, and a settled result refunds only after its 
claim deadline

Once the result is posted, rebuild it from public data (the final kit, every final action log and the export of the 
entries) and compare it with the escrow; if it differs, challenge it with the bond before the challenge window ends:

