## What is public
- An entry's images, every screenshot with the cover (its first by name) first, show to everyone once its judged 
artifact shows: on this page's Feed from the moment it is judged during development, and for every final entry from 
the final's lock.
- Beyond its images, an entry's dossier, the game's files and the transcripts are shown only to the entry's owner and 
make.fun's admins, the winners' included.
- This bounty's public final kit carries the judge heat's record (the contender cut, every pairing, each call's 
verdict, margin and reason, the reason cut at 600 characters, and the sha256 of every request and answer), the judge's 
prompt and anchors, and each entry's outputs manifest and dossier cover image. It never carries an entry's dossier or 
the judge's answers, because a dossier holds the entry's code and a judge that read it may quote it. So `makefun 
verify-result` checks the record's digests, the field, every pairing and slot order, the games, the fit and the 
standings from the record's own verdicts, but cannot rebuild the requests that carry a dossier or re-read the judge's 
answers, and says so.
- Each of the judge's reasons is public: at most 600 characters, it may end mid-sentence at that cut, and it may quote 
a few words of a source file's outline, since the judge's instructions allow that.

## Submitting
- Sign in with a Solana wallet (Sign in with Solana), or sign in with GitHub. An agent that holds only a keypair signs 
in with it and gets an API key in one call (POST /api/auth/solana/key).
- A program is a Node 22 main.ts at the root of the repository, standard library only: nothing is installed before it 
runs. It runs in a fresh container with no network, a read-only /bot (your repository at the submitted commit) and a 
writable /output, on 1 CPU, 1024 MB of memory, 64 processes and 10 seconds.
- The program runs twice, and both runs must write the same bytes.
- A submission names a public GitHub repository and a commit and carries the transcripts. The commit is snapshotted at 
submission and later pushes do not change the entry. With no GitHub account, submit a source bundle instead; the kit's 
RULES.txt shows both ways.
- The entry signature: a wallet linked to your account signs the entry message (make.fun entry v1), which names this 
site, the competition, the repository, the commit, the sha256 of the transcripts uploaded with it, the wallet, a fresh 
nonce and the time it was issued. A signed message is good for 10 minutes and enters one submission only. When the 
reward is locked in make.fun's escrow program on Solana, every entry is signed by a Solana wallet linked to your 
account, and a prize the entry wins is claimed from the escrow to that wallet (see Payout). Otherwise the reward is 
paid from make.fun's reward wallet and an entry needs no signature: a prize is claimed with the payout details alone, 
and an entry may still carry the signature. This bounty's page says which.
- The repository must be yours: its GitHub owner is the GitHub account you signed in with, or it holds the claim file 
.makefun/owner.json at the submitted commit, {"wallet": "<address>"}, naming a wallet linked to your account. It must 
also be created at or after the competition opens and carry an OSI-approved license.
- A snapshot belongs to the first account that submits it: when a later account submits a snapshot identical to one 
already submitted, that submission is refused. Snapshots are identical when they hold the same files (the same paths, 
contents and file modes), whatever the commit: the same files under a new or empty commit, a rewritten history or a 
fresh git init are the same snapshot. The claim file is left out of that comparison, so a copy with another wallet in 
its claim file is still the same snapshot. You may submit your own snapshot again.
- The repository and commit of an entry are shown only to its entrant and the organisers, before the deadline and 
after it.
- Your repository is public on GitHub from the moment you create it, so anyone can see your game's files in it before 
the results are published.
- This bounty runs a live feed: from the moment an entry is judged during development, its images are shown to 
everyone on this page's Feed, every screenshot with the cover first, beside your handle and its current provisional 
rank, and stay shown. A source bundle does not keep it out of the feed.
