 succeeded in 544ms:
- Each entry's score is its win rate: a Bradley-Terry fit over every game of the final heat, each game counting its 
score as a share of a win, gives each entry in the heat a strength, and its win rate is its expected share of wins 
against every other member of the heat. A cut entry keeps the numbers of its development rate, over no final game.
- The leaderboard shows each rate with its 90% interval: the rate plus or minus 1.6449 times its standard error, kept 
within 0 and 1. Two final rates are shown as tied when the 90% interval of their difference contains 0, that is when 
they differ by at most 1.6449 times the square root of the sum of their squared standard errors. A provisional rate is 
never shown as tied. Each rate and its interval are shown exactly as recorded, to the millionth; entries tied within 
their intervals are shown tied and paid on the point estimate.
- Places go by the score, best first. The place, and with it any reward, follows the recorded point estimate, the rate 
itself, after two rules: the entries that played the playoff place above every entry that did not, and every entry 
judged in the final heat places above every cut entry, whatever the rates. Within each group the higher rate places 
first. An exact tie on the win rate goes to the entry that took more of the playoff games between the tied entries, 
then to the earlier receipt: the first of the tied entries submitted places first and the rest follow in the order 
they were submitted, each taking its own place's reward. A displayed tie never moves a place.
- Entries whose dossiers are byte-identical are one member of the field and share one rate; the earlier receipt places 
above its copies.

## Finalist review
Once the final heat settles, each entrant's entry in places 1 to 3 is held, keeping its row but no place while it 
waits, for at most 30 minutes. In that time the make.fun team may disqualify an entry that is not a playable game or 
that copies another, with a reason (out of the standings, and the next entry takes its place), or clear it early (it 
keeps its place). While the 30 minutes run, an entry a disqualification moves into places 1 to 3 is held too. An entry 
nobody has decided when the 30 minutes lapse is cleared by rule and keeps its place, so the results never wait longer 
and need nobody to act. Nothing else runs the game before a reward is paid: the gate reads its files only, and the 
screenshots the judge sees are the entrant's own.

## Rewards
- 1st place: $12
- 2nd place: $8
- 3rd place: $6
- 4th place: $5
- 5th place: $4
- 6th to 10th place: $3 each

The rewards total $50, paid by the house in USDC on Solana (see Payout). They go to the 10 highest-ranked entries of 
the final heat, one place per entrant. An entry the gate refused, an entry the transcript gate rejected and a cut 
entry take no place. A house bot, an entry make.fun enters itself, ranks in the heat like any other entry. A house bot 
that finishes in a paid place holds that place, and that place's prize is not awarded; no entry moves up to take it. 
Any place that no entry is left to take is not awarded.

